{"ts":"2026-05-25T20:47:07Z","hook":"PreToolUse","tool":"exec","decision":"approve","reason":"default allow","command":"cd /Users/meilynlopezcubero/antigravity/Faithful && git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
fix(renderer): disable deferred lighting pipeline for PIXI v8 compatibility

PIXI v8 changed the Shader/UniformGroup resource API. The deferred
lighting quad shader was throwing "Cannot create property 'name' on
number '1'" during init, causing the entire renderer to fail and the
world to render as black.

Changes:
- Wrap deferred lighting Shader/Mesh creation in try-catch
- Fall back to direct stage rendering when deferred pipeline fails
- Remove debug stack trace logging added during investigation

The terrain, entities, and UI now render correctly.

Generated with [Devin](https://cli.devin.ai/docs)

Co-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
EOF
)" -a"}
