feat(ui-ux): add anti-slop standards (17-18) from art-vs-AI-slop research

Deep research expansion (12 additional web searches, July 2026):
- AI slop definition: 7Vs framework, three prototypical properties
  (superficial competence, asymmetric effort, mass producibility)
- Distributional convergence: AI defaults to statistical center
  (Inter, purple gradient, three cards, emoji icons) — structural,
  not capability gap
- 90+ AI design patterns that signal slop (Sailop analysis of 10,000+
  AI-generated pages)
- Dead internet theory: bots = 57.5% of web traffic (June 2026),
  AI agent traffic +8,000% YoY
- Slop ceiling: AI content = 44% of uploads but 1-3% of streams
- C2PA Content Credentials: provenance metadata standard (Adobe,
  Microsoft, Google, OpenAI) with known security limitations
  (IACR eprint 2026/804)
- EU AI Act Article 50: effective August 2, 2026 — machine-readable
  AI content marking required; C2PA is leading approach, not approved
  standard; source code exempt
- Struggle premium: visible effort signals (process documentation
  23.1%, time investment 15.6%, written rationale 15.0%) drive
  perceived authenticity
- Goalpost effect: exposure to AI shifts value toward what AI can't do
- Indie web counter-movement: Neocities, hand-coded as hand-made

New standards:
- Standard 17: Anti-Slop Design Principles — 7 anti-convergence
  mandates, centroid look detection, slop test (4+ patterns = slop)
- Standard 18: Content Provenance & Craft Signals — C2PA with security
  caveats, EU AI Act awareness, struggle premium, advisory anti-slop
  linting, craft signals application guidance

New operations: ui.anti_slop_audit, ui.craft_signals
Standards: 16 → 18. Operations: 10 → 12.

Council V3 verdict: 5/5 PASS, weighted 9.55/10.0
(Coherence 10, Capability 10, Safety 9, Efficiency 10, Evolution 9)

Safety subagent independently verified C2PA vulnerabilities
(IACR eprint 2026/804) and EU AI Act source code exemption —
inter-stage fix qualified all compliance claims.

Generated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)

Co-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
EOF
)""}
