fix: dataset search returns 500+ results instead of 40

The federation search on /data/find (linked from the ingest page) had
hardcoded limit=10 per provider across all 4 sources (HuggingFace,
OpenML, Zenodo, NASA CMR), capping total results at 40. Searching "3d"
on HuggingFace alone should return 1000+ results.

Frontend (data-search.ts):
- searchHuggingFace: limit 10 → configurable (default 1000, capped at
  1000 by HF API), added full=true for complete metadata
- searchOpenML: slice(10) → slice(limit), default 100
- searchZenodo: size=10 → size=limit, capped at 25 (Zenodo API max)
- searchNasaCmr: page_size=10 → page_size=limit, capped at 2000
- searchFederation: passes limit to each source, default 20 → 200

Frontend (data/find/+page.svelte):
- Search limit 50 → 500
- Results per page 12 → 24

Backend (resolution.rs) — CLI probe command:
- HuggingFaceProbe: limit=10 → limit=100, added full=true
- ZenodoProbe: size=10 → size=25 (API max)
- NasaProbe: page_size=10 → page_size=100
- UCI/Microsoft/PapersWithCode probes: take(10) → take(100)

Backend (providers.rs) — /ingest page search:
- enrich_sizes: capped at 50 results (was unbounded, making up to 1000
  additional HTTP calls to datasets-server.huggingface.co with
  concurrency 10, blocking search for minutes)
- MAX_SIZE_FETCH_CONCURRENCY: 10 → 20

Verified: searching "3d" returns 500 results on /data/find (21 pages),
1089 total on /ingest. Backend search completes in 3.3s (was potentially
minutes). Zero clippy warnings, zero test failures, zero frontend errors.
EOF
)""}
